    "confidence": 0.39,
    "explanation": "Both parties: this case turns on one stretch of road the evidence cannot see, so it goes to a human reviewer and the disputed $34.42 is held rather than collected or refunded.\n\nThe trip is TRP-00110, Compass One (Sengkang) to Marina Bay Financial Centre, charged $34.42 (EV-FARE-00110, charged_total). The platform's booked optimal is 18.4 km and 26.0 min (EV-TRIP-00110). The measured distance is 21.2 km, an excess of 2.8 km or 15.2% (EV-GPS-00110, derived.deviation), which on its face falls short of POL-RD-01's two gates (excess must exceed both 20% of optimal and 0.8 km).\n\nWhy that measurement cannot decide the case. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00110 is impaired, weight 0.39, issue codes GPS_GAP and LOW_COVERAGE: a single 428-second dropout from 18:35:00 to 18:42:08, bounded by fixes 6.90 km apart in a straight line, covering exactly the KPE tunnel stretch in dispute. That is over POL-RD-07's 90-second limb, so the trace is impaired for POLICY purposes and not merely down-weighted by the admissibility pre-pass. POL-RD-07(i) measures the gap as the straight line between the bounding fixes — the reading most favourable to the driver — and that is where 21.2 km comes from. But that figure is a floor, not a measurement: the admissibility record states a surface route between the same two portals would put the trip at 25.50 km, which would exceed the POL-RD-01 gate. Nothing in the bundle distinguishes the two readings.\n\nUnder POL-RD-07(ii) a deviation may not be established on an impaired trace alone; it needs an independent source — a driver admission in the chat log, erp_gantries placing the vehicle off the optimal corridor, a counterparty statement admitting the route, or a trip_record distance derived independently of the trace. None exists. The chat log EV-CHAT-00110 (impaired, weight 0.6, issue code TRUNCATED_LOG — the export stops at 18:26:14) contains no admission, only the driver's \"going KPE ah boss\" and the rider's \"ok\", both consistent with the booked optimal corridor (KPE then ECP per EV-TRIP-00110). The fare breakdown's erp_gantries is null, so the gantry route check cannot be run. trip_record.actual_distance_km (21.2) and distance_charged_km (21.2) are copies of the same trace figure, which POL-RD-07(ii) expressly excludes as circular. The driver's counterparty statement, \"I took the KPE like always\", admits the optimal route, not a deviation.\n\nThat is the mandatory escalation. POL-RD-07(iii) directs that absence of proof on an impaired trace is a data failure, not a finding for the driver, and the outcome is ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION; POL-RD-10(3) makes that mandatory. Independently, POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence in any ruling on the excess at 0.39, the weight of the artifact carrying it (EV-GPS-00110, whose 21.2 km the trip record and fare ledger merely copy — one measurement, not independent carriers), which is below the platform floor of 0.70, so POL-RD-10(1) fires as well. Reported confidence is therefore 0.39.\n\nThe driver's contrary claims are answered. That the straight-line reading falls below the POL-RD-01 gate is true but cannot carry NO_ACTION: it is the most driver-favourable reading of an impaired stretch, it is a floor, and the clause governing an impaired trace directs escalation rather than a finding. The point that the rider's own 18–19 km estimate also falls short is arithmetic on that same unusable measurement. The submission that the driver ran the optimal corridor rests on the routing-engine text on EV-TRIP-00110, not on a fix inside the tunnel, and cannot resolve what happened there. I accept that no repeat-deviation pattern is established (POL-RD-06: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 744), so no FULL_REFUND uplift under (b) and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arise. The $3.00 ERP stands as charged: erp_gantries is null, so under POL-RD-09(4) the gantry match is undecidable, the line is treated as matched, and no billing-integrity finding or referral arises. POL-RD-05 is unavailable — pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null, as are the amended optimal fields — so no part of the excess is excluded on that ground. I accept that the rider's enhanced-corroboration requirement under POL-RD-08 is not engaged (EV-RPROF-00110: deviation_claims_60d 1, substantiated 0, far below 4). EV-ADVIS-00110-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, so POL-RD-03 is unavailable to the driver.\n\nEscalation is terminal and replaces the ruling: no money moves and the disputed amount is held. What would resolve it: a GPS fix, gantry record or independent running-distance measurement inside the 18:35:00–18:42:08 window, or any running distance not derived from this trace."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "These three artifacts describe one and the same trip: EV-TRIP-00110 (trip_record), EV-GPS-00110 (gps_trace) and EV-FARE-00110 (fare_breakdown) each carry trip_id TRP-00110 and the same accepted/start window on 22 July 2026. The first limb of the rider's burden under POL-RD-08(a) is therefore satisfied and the tribunal can move to the excess question.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00110 at weight_multiplier 0.39 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Even measured the POL-RD-07(i) way - the straight line across the bounding fixes, the reading most favourable to the driver - the excess on EV-GPS-00110 comes out at 2.8 km, 15.2% of the 18.4 km optimal carried on EV-TRIP-00110. That figure is a floor on the distance driven across the gap, not a measurement of it: the admissibility record for EV-GPS-00110 states that a surface route between the same two portals would put the trip at 25.50 km, which is over the POL-RD-01 gate. Nothing in the bundle distinguishes the two readings, so the threshold test cannot be safely run either way.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00110 at weight_multiplier 0.39 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The reason the driver cannot be contradicted in chat is a platform failure, not a rider failure: EV-CHAT-00110 is flagged truncated and its last_message_at is 18:26:14, 2186 seconds before the trip ended at 19:02:40. Everything said while the vehicle was inside the disputed tunnel segment is simply absent from the export, so the missing corroboration is a data gap on the record before us.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-CHAT-00110 at weight_multiplier 0.6 but does not name its issue code(s): TRUNCATED_LOG"
    },
    {
      "claim": "No traffic advisory covers the KPE or the ECP in the 18:19-19:02 window: EV-ADVIS-00110-01 is MISSING, a null payload at weight 0.0. Its absence is itself citable, and it means POL-RD-03 is unavailable to the driver - neither the extra distance nor the duration overrun can be laid at the door of a closure on this record.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00110-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "POL-RD-04 is likewise unavailable to the driver. The rider gave no detour instruction: both messages on EV-CHAT-00110 carry waypoint_hint null, no road is named by the rider, and the rider's 'ok' merely answers the driver's own 'going KPE', which is the booked optimal corridor described on EV-TRIP-00110 as KPE then ECP, not a departure from it. There is nothing to exonerate on this limb.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-CHAT-00110 at weight_multiplier 0.6 but does not name its issue code(s): TRUNCATED_LOG"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The $34.42 charge rests on the same single impaired measurement the rider is contesting. distance_charged_km of 21.20 on EV-FARE-00110 is identical to the 21.20 trace figure on EV-GPS-00110, and the platform's own pre-pass says so, so the ledger adds no independent evidence of distance. EV-FARE-00110 is impaired at 0.75 with issue code PARTIAL_RECORD. A charge whose only basis is an artifact that cannot see the disputed segment is not a charge the rider should be left carrying.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00110 at weight_multiplier 0.39 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The duration is unexplained on this record. EV-TRIP-00110 records actual_duration_min of 39.0 against a booked optimal of 26.0 on a corridor the platform itself calls KPE then ECP - half again as long. With EV-ADVIS-00110-01 absent, erp_gantries null and the chat truncated, nothing in the bundle accounts for that overrun, and it is a further reason the present record cannot settle whether the vehicle stayed on the booked corridor.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00110-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "On this record the correct outcome is ESCALATE, not NO_ACTION. The trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c); no corroborating artifact of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names exists; and POL-RD-07(iii) directs that absence of proof on an impaired trace is a data failure rather than a finding for the driver. POL-RD-10(3) makes that escalation mandatory, and escalation holds the disputed $34.42 rather than collecting it.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00110 at weight_multiplier 0.39 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The trace is impaired FOR POLICY PURPOSES under POL-RD-07(a): a single 428-second gap between consecutive fixes, far over the clause's 90-second limb, bounded by the Defu Flyover and Kallang portal fixes and covering the entire segment the rider disputes. POL-RD-07(i) directs that excess across an impaired stretch be measured as the straight line between the bounding fixes - expressly 'the reading most favourable to the driver' - and on that reading the trip is 21.2 km, below the POL-RD-01 threshold. Correctly applied, the impairment confirms the no-deviation result rather than disturbing it.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00110 at weight_multiplier 0.39 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The rider bears the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and must show an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold, measured from an unimpaired trace or from an independent source named in POL-RD-07(ii). He has neither: the only distance measurement in the bundle is the impaired trace, and its prescribed reading gives 2.8 km / 15.2%, under the gate. His complaint that the timing 'does not make sense' is a duration point, and duration appears nowhere in POL-RD-01's establishment test - a slow run on a correctly followed corridor is not a route deviation. No burden ever shifts to the driver.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00110 at weight_multiplier 0.39 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE"
    },
    {
      "claim": "In the alternative, if the tunnel dropout is held to leave the excess genuinely unmeasurable, the only permissible route is ESCALATE, not a refund. POL-RD-07(ii)-(iii) require independent corroboration of any deviation and direct ESCALATE where none exists: the truncated chat contains no driver admission, erp_gantries is null, and trip_record.actual_distance_km is a copy of the impaired trace, so no POL-RD-07(ii) source is available. Under POL-RD-10(3) the disputed amount is then held rather than refunded while a human reviews it. Either way the driver is not required to return the fare.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00110 at weight_multiplier 0.39 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE"
    }
  ]
}
